Package: Briones
Type: Package
Title: Choropleth Maps of San Francisco Supervisor Districts
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Steve", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "steve.the.bayesian@gmail.com")
Author: Steve [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Steve <steve.the.bayesian@gmail.com>
Description: Draws the eleven San Francisco Board of Supervisors districts as a
    choropleth (filled) map, shading each district according to a numeric value
    supplied in a data frame. Colour gradients are specified the same way as in
    'image' and 'heatmap': a vector of colours plus optional 'zlim' or 'breaks'.
    District boundaries are bundled with the package, so no network access,
    spatial libraries or external dependencies are required. Uses base graphics
    only.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
LazyData: true
NeedsCompilation: no
